best_response:
 Your implementation is a good starting point for finding unique words between two texts in MATLAB. However, it can be further optimized by avoiding reading the texts directly into memory using the `fileread` function if the files are too large. Instead, use the `textscan` function to read the lines one by one and process them in batches. Here's the updated code:
```matlab
% Open files for reading
fid1 = fopen('Text1.txt','r');
fid2 = fopen('Text2.txt','r');
% Initialize empty cell arrays for storing words
words1 = {};
words2 = {};
% Read lines in batches and process words
while ~feof(fid1) && ~feof(fid2)
    line1 = fgets(fid1, Inf, '.'); % read line from Text1
    line2 = fgets(fid2, Inf, '.'); % read line from Text2

    % Convert text to lowercase and split into words
    words1Temp = lower(strsplit(line1));
    words2Temp = lower(strsplit(line2));

    % Combine words with existing ones
    words1 = [words1; words1Temp];
    words2 = [words2; words2Temp];
end
% Close files
fclose(fid1);
fclose(fid2);
% Find unique words in text1 that do not appear in text2
uniqueWords = setdiff(words1, words2);
% Print the unique words
disp(uniqueWords);
```
This implementation reads the lines one by one and processes them in batches, which is more memory-efficient when dealing with large texts.

