 To write a C++ program for bubble sort algorithm using minimal memory and avoiding potential errors, follow the steps below:

1. Define a function to perform bubble sort:
```cpp
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;
void bubbleSort(int arr[], int n) {
    for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {
        for (int j = 0; j < n - i - 1; j++) {
            if (arr[j] > arr[j+1]) {
                swap(arr[j], arr[j+1]);
            }
        }
    }
}
```

2. Create a main function to read JSON data, call bubbleSort(), and display sorted data:
